    {
      "id": "rust-chain",
      "seconds": 16,
      "heading": "Iterator chains",
      "narration": "Modern languages can describe this too. Rust has iterator chains. Map, then filter, then sum. The difference is not that Rust cannot map or reduce. In an array language, arrays and their operations are the center of the language.",
      "lines": [],
      "panel": {
        "type": "code",
        "lines": [
          {
            "code": "let total: i32 = values"
          },
          {
            "code": "    .iter()"
          },
          {
            "code": "    .map(|x| x * 3)"
          },
          {
            "code": "    .filter(|x| *x > 5)"
          },
          {
            "code": "    .sum();"
          },
          {
            "code": "// 60"
          }
        ],
        "focus": [
          [],
          [
            0,
            1
          ],
          [
            2,
